Tibetan Buddhism is based on the teachings of the Buddha, but additionally includes the path of Mahayana love and numerous techniques of Indian yoga.
Tibetan Buddhism is very simple. It consists of Kundalini yoga, meditation and the path of all-encompassing love.
Kundalini yoga causes the energy of kundalini (i.e. the energy of enlightenment) to awaken by practicing asanas, breathing exercises, mantras and visualizations.
In the center of Tibetan meditation there is deity yoga. Thanks to the visualization of various deities, energy channels are purified, chakras are activated and enlightenment is created.
