Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in the north-east of South Africa, bordering in the east with Mozambique, in the north of Zimbabwe, and the southern border is marked by the Crocodile River.
The area of the park covers 19 500 km2 and is divided into 14 different ecozones, characterized by different flora and fauna.
It is one of the biggest attractions in South Africa and is considered the flagship among South African national parks (SANPArks).
There are fees for daily protection and access to the park, as in all other South African national parks.
Purchasing a wild card can be beneficial, as it allows access to selected parks in South Africa or to all South African national parks.
