Europe is a relatively small continent, but with many independent countries. Under normal circumstances, travelling through several countries would mean having to apply for multiple visas and multiple passport controls.
In this respect, the Schengen area functions to some extent like one country.
As long as you remain in this zone, you can generally cross borders without going through passport checkpoints again.
In the same way, you do not have to submit a separate visa application to each of the Schengen Member States, which allows you to save time and money and reduce formalities.
