Difficult weather conditions are a general definition of any dangerous atmospheric phenomenon, which may result in damage, serious disruption of social life or the death of people.
Difficult weather conditions can occur anywhere in the world and can vary, depending on geographical location, topography and weather conditions.
The manifestations and effects of difficult weather conditions include gusty winds, hail, violent downpours, uncontrolled fires, thunderstorms, tornadoes, whirlwinds and cyclones.
Extreme seasonal weather conditions in the region are m.in. blizzards, snowstorms, ice storms and dusting.
It is recommended that travelers pay attention to the risk of adverse weather conditions in their area, as they can affect their travel plans.
