Christmas, commemorating the coming of Jesus into the world, is one of the most important Christian holidays.
Unbelievers in Christian countries and people of other faiths around the world have incorporated many traditions into their lives, with which these holidays grew.
According to a certain tradition, Easter night is spent, waking in an uncovered place and waiting for the sunrise.
Of course, there are Christian theological explanations of this tradition, but it might as well be the pre-Christian ritual of spring and fertility.
Churches with a more traditional approach celebrate the liturgy of the Easter Vigil in the evening on Holy Saturday, and the faithful often begin to celebrate the resurrection of Christ when the clock strikes midnight.
