Japanese work culture is more hierarchical and formal than the work culture to which Westerners are accustomed.
Suit is a standard business outfit, and co-workers turn to each other by name or use a business title.
Harmony in the workplace is essential and emphasizes group effort rather than individual achievements.
Employees usually have to obtain the consent of superiors in order to be able to make a decision on their own, they also have to follow orders without any questions.
